 dict(chainIds=[99901, 4663, 5042, 196, 1], lens='L4', question='For the launch pad hooks that keep fee ledgers and reject a direct initialize (0x6b1216a40b65c83e9c9e18a562c446697b8cf8ec, 0xe0def4221b9840a610d4e7d55812a79a6431a8ec and 0x3ab88ddc3cf2a012af88b60828edb4553697e5dc on Elysium, CashCatHookV2, PonsV2MemeHook, 0x4eb1976978756bd56802d8162f2271844924e0cc and 0x2c668601193e4a081dd82604785e436aff6a2acc on Robinhood Chain, WonkHook and MinaraFeeHook on Arc, TaxLaunchHook on X Layer, LaunchHook on Ethereum): can an ordinary account launch through the factory with a quote currency of its choice, and is each fee ledger stored per pool id or per token and currency?', why='The Klik finding is a ledger stored per token and paid in the currency of the calling pool. Hooks that hold claims for thousands of pools and let the launcher pick the quote currency can have the same fault behind a factory gate. These hooks hold claims or balances today, for example 178 native units and 20.5 native claims at the first Elysium hook.', priority='medium'),
